From 7e5e646b23d3c7a50fbee47edadb810439f10080 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 07:08:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(2d): fence the whole-contour lead room at a level another
 band shares

A grown outline that takes the levels above its first level shares a
plane with a ring of an earlier band (Top Z when the stock top stands one
stepdown or more over it). A lead longer than the gap between the two
rings crossed the other ring at that plane, and the verifier's Crossing
law blocked the post.

The whole-model contour now plans its bands first and emits them at the
end. Each band's lead room is its center plus a thin fence around each
ring of another band cut on a shared level, so the lead fitter shortens,
reseats or refuses the lead by name. The levels do not change. Errors
with a partial path emit the planned bands first.

Fixes #2677

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
